issue.body:
Given the following code:

```php
try {
    $container->get('dependency');
} catch (ContainerExceptionInterface $exception) {
    Log::to('error')->error($exception->getMessage());
}
```

`ContainerExceptionInterface` is the PSR-11 one, found here: [php-fig/container](https://github.com/php-fig/container/blob/master/src/ContainerExceptionInterface.php). Psalm gives an `UndefinedMethod` error (for `getMessage()` on `$exception`). This is technically correct, because if it's purely inferred from the interface, it has no methods (the `ContainerExceptionInterface` cannot extend `Throwable` because it would break compatibility with everything < PHP 7.0.

Since every exception thrown implements `Throwable` by definition (as far as I know), I would consider it a false positive.
